    "raw_text": "\nmulti-dimensional analysis:\nLet me analyze this video based on the provided frames and the text prompt.\n\nThe text prompt asks for: \"生成一段15秒、1:1方形画幅的微缩模型定格动画宠物生活纪录，采用微缩模型定格动画风格\" (Generate a 15-second, 1:1 square format micro-model stop-motion animation pet life record in micro-model stop-motion style).\n\nLooking at the frames:\n\nVisual Quality Analysis:\n- The frames depict an orange tabby cat on a beige cushion/ottoman with a woman seated nearby.\n- The resolution is solid; lighting is warm and natural, with consistent color grading across shots.\n- The cat's fur texture and whiskers are clearly visible; the woman's features are discernible.\n- Transitions between frames are smooth; no obvious artifacts or distortions; overall image quality is good but not exceptional.\n\nText-to-Video Alignment Analysis:\n- The prompt specifies a 15-second, 1:1 square format micro-model stop-motion animation of pet life. The footage shows a real cat and a person, not a micro-model setup, so it does not fulfill the micro-model stop-motion requirement.\n- The framing is not consistently 1:1 square; most shots are wides or standard aspect.\n- The content aligns more with a standard pet-life scene than with a stylized micro-model animation.\n- Overall alignment to the requested micro-model stop-motion prompt is limited.\n\nPhysical Consistency / Common-sense:\n- Cat movements appear natural; interactions with the environment are plausible; lighting and shadows stay coherent; no obvious physics violations.\n- The scene remains believable as a real-world cat-and-human interaction.\n\nOverall assessment:\n- Visual quality is solid and coherent, with good detail and lighting.\n- Text-to-video alignment is limited due to missing key prompt elements (micro-model stop-motion and exact framing).\n- Physical/common-sense consistency is strong, with natural motion and plausible interactions.\n\n</think>\n\n(1) visual quality: 4\n(2) text-to-video alignment: 2\n(3) physical/common-sense consistency: 4\n"
